      "path": "src/persistence/persistence.ts",
      "content": "A synchronous error inside this async function becomes a rejected promise without aborting the IndexedDB transaction. For example, `key: NaN` is allowed by the TypeScript `IDBValidKey` type but makes `IDBKeyRange.only` throw `DataError`. The request catch below swallows that rejection, while `tx.done` can still resolve, so preceding writes persist and commit returns `Committed` even though this operation failed. Construct the range and issue the initial cursor request synchronously inside the outer try, or explicitly abort the transaction when the cursor task rejects.",
      "existing_code": "            request = (async () =\u003e {\n              let cursor = await index.openCursor(IDBKeyRange.only(write.key));\n              while (cursor) cursor = await cursor.continue();\n            })();",
